authlib-injector
================

This directory bundles `authlib-injector.jar`, a third-party Java agent used by
Histolauncher to redirect Minecraft's authentication and texture endpoints to
the local skin/cape proxy.

Project:    authlib-injector
Author:     Haowei Wen (yushijinhun) and contributors
Homepage:   https://github.com/yushijinhun/authlib-injector
Version:    1.2.8 (upstream), with the Histolauncher patch applied
License:    GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 or later
            (AGPL-3.0-or-later), with the "AUTHLIB-INJECTOR" exception
License:    https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.html


Modified binary
---------------

The jar shipped here is NOT the stock upstream release. Five classes are
replaced with Histolauncher builds:

	moe.yushi.authlibinjector.httpd.DefaultURLRedirector
	moe.yushi.authlibinjector.transform.support.AccountTypeTransformer
	moe.yushi.authlibinjector.transform.support.AuthServerNameInjector
	moe.yushi.authlibinjector.transform.support.ConstantURLTransformUnit
	moe.yushi.authlibinjector.transform.support.YggdrasilKeyTransformUnit

Every other class is the unmodified upstream binary. A patched jar can be
identified by the `Histolauncher-Patched` attribute in its `META-INF/MANIFEST.MF`.

Because the bundled binary is modified, clause 1 of the AUTHLIB-INJECTOR
exception (which covers bundling the *unaltered* binary) does not apply to it,
and the corresponding source for the modification must be made available. The
complete source of the modified classes, together with the build script that
reproduces this jar from a stock upstream release, is published at:

	https://github.com/KerbalOfficial/Histolauncher
	-> tools/authlib-injector-histolauncher-patch/

That directory is part of the public Histolauncher repository but is not
included in packaged Histolauncher releases, because release packaging only
ships the `src/` tree. The repository above is the offer of corresponding
source required by section 6 of the AGPL.


AUTHLIB-INJECTOR exception (upstream text)
------------------------------------------

	As a special exception, using this work in the following ways does not
	cause your program to be covered by the AGPL:

	1. Bundling the unaltered binary form of this work in your program
	   without statically or dynamically linking to it; or
	2. Interacting with this work through the provided inter-process
	   communication interface, such as the HTTP API; or
	3. Loading this work as a Java Agent into a Java Virtual Machine.

Histolauncher loads authlib-injector as a Java Agent (clause 3) and talks to it
over the local HTTP API (clause 2), so Histolauncher's own code remains under
its own license. See the top-level LICENSE file.


